casebook b-46cfr-58_25-25-steering-alarms-draft v1
source "B-46cfr-58.25-25-steering-alarms.txt" dated 2026-10-14 by "drafted by anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5 from the manual; not yet approved"
note "UNAPPROVED DRAFT: written by a language model from B-46cfr-58.25-25-steering-alarms.txt. Every declaration below cites the sentence"
note "it came from. Check each against the manual, add what the manual does not say, then delete"
note "this note to approve. quorum studio will not build a chip image while it is here."

# manual: "Failure of the electric power to the control system of any steering gear"
observe control_power_lost "electric power to the control system of a steering gear has failed"

# manual: "Failure of that power to the power unit of any steering gear"
observe power_unit_power_lost "electric power to the power unit of a steering gear has failed"

# manual: "Occurrence of a low oil level in any oil reservoir of a hydraulic, power-operated steering-gear system"
observe low_oil_level "low oil level in a reservoir of a hydraulic, power-operated steering-gear system"

# manual: "Failure of any phase of a three-phase power supply"
observe phase_lost "a phase of a three-phase power supply has failed"

# manual: "Overload of any motor described by § 58.25-55(c)"
observe motor_overloaded "a steering-gear motor is overloaded"

# manual: "that activates when the motor is energized"
observe motor_energized "a power motor for the main or auxiliary steering gear is energized"

# manual: "Failure of the electric power to the control system of any steering gear"
claim control_power_failure "control system power failure on a steering gear" severity 6 needs control_power_lost

# manual: "Failure of that power to the power unit of any steering gear"
claim power_unit_failure "power unit power failure on a steering gear" severity 6 needs power_unit_power_lost

# manual: "Occurrence of a low oil level in any oil reservoir of a hydraulic, power-operated steering-gear system"
claim low_oil "low oil level in a hydraulic steering-gear reservoir" severity 5 needs low_oil_level

# manual: "Failure of any phase of a three-phase power supply"
claim phase_failure "failure of a phase of the three-phase supply" severity 5 needs phase_lost

# manual: "Overload of any motor described by § 58.25-55(c)"
claim motor_overload "overload of a steering-gear motor" severity 5 needs motor_overloaded

# manual: "Each power motor for the main and auxiliary steering gear must have a “motor running” indicator light in the pilothouse, and in the machinery space, that activates when the motor is energized"
claim motor_running "a steering-gear power motor is running and must be indicated" severity 1 needs motor_energized

# manual: "An audible and a visible alarm must activate in the pilothouse upon"
action alarm_pilothouse when any control_power_failure power_unit_failure low_oil low_oil_level_blind

# manual: "An audible and a visible alarm must activate in the machinery space upon"
action alarm_machinery_space when any phase_failure motor_overload low_oil phase_lost_blind motor_overloaded_blind

# manual: "that activates when the motor is energized"
action normal_operation idle

# manual: "must have a “motor running” indicator light in the pilothouse, and in the machinery space"
action show_motor_running when any motor_running motor_energized_blind

# manual: "a steering-failure alarm must be provided in the pilothouse"
action steer_safe_state safe when any control_power_failure power_unit_failure control_power_lost_blind power_unit_power_lost_blind

# manual: "must have a “motor running” indicator light in the pilothouse, and in the machinery space"
prefer steer_safe_state over alarm_pilothouse over alarm_machinery_space over show_motor_running over normal_operation

# ── Failed-sensor checks, added by quorum studio ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# cbc refused this rulebook because nothing could argue with any claim, so it could not tell a dead sensor
# from a quiet machine. Each block below stops claims being drawn from one reading while its instrument has
# failed, and takes the response that reading would have led to instead. Each is a suggestion: confirm or
# delete it.

# TODO: confirm the device can tell when the control_power_lost instrument has failed (a broken wire, a stuck
# or out-of-range value), and that steer_safe_state is the right response then. If control_power_lost is not an
# instrument at all, delete these lines.
observe control_power_lost_failed "the instrument behind control_power_lost has failed or is disconnected"
doubt control_power_lost_untrusted "control_power_lost is not trusted while its instrument has failed" needs control_power_lost_failed
control_power_lost_untrusted undercuts control_power_failure
claim control_power_lost_blind "there is no trustworthy reading of control_power_lost" needs control_power_lost_failed

# TODO: confirm the device can tell when the power_unit_power_lost instrument has failed (a broken wire, a stuck
# or out-of-range value), and that steer_safe_state is the right response then. If power_unit_power_lost is not an
# instrument at all, delete these lines.
observe power_unit_power_lost_failed "the instrument behind power_unit_power_lost has failed or is disconnected"
doubt power_unit_power_lost_untrusted "power_unit_power_lost is not trusted while its instrument has failed" needs power_unit_power_lost_failed
power_unit_power_lost_untrusted undercuts power_unit_failure
claim power_unit_power_lost_blind "there is no trustworthy reading of power_unit_power_lost" needs power_unit_power_lost_failed

# TODO: confirm the device can tell when the low_oil_level instrument has failed (a broken wire, a stuck
# or out-of-range value), and that alarm_pilothouse is the right response then. If low_oil_level is not an
# instrument at all, delete these lines.
observe low_oil_level_failed "the instrument behind low_oil_level has failed or is disconnected"
doubt low_oil_level_untrusted "low_oil_level is not trusted while its instrument has failed" needs low_oil_level_failed
low_oil_level_untrusted undercuts low_oil
claim low_oil_level_blind "there is no trustworthy reading of low_oil_level" needs low_oil_level_failed

# TODO: confirm the device can tell when the phase_lost instrument has failed (a broken wire, a stuck
# or out-of-range value), and that alarm_machinery_space is the right response then. If phase_lost is not an
# instrument at all, delete these lines.
observe phase_lost_failed "the instrument behind phase_lost has failed or is disconnected"
doubt phase_lost_untrusted "phase_lost is not trusted while its instrument has failed" needs phase_lost_failed
phase_lost_untrusted undercuts phase_failure
claim phase_lost_blind "there is no trustworthy reading of phase_lost" needs phase_lost_failed

# TODO: confirm the device can tell when the motor_overloaded instrument has failed (a broken wire, a stuck
# or out-of-range value), and that alarm_machinery_space is the right response then. If motor_overloaded is not an
# instrument at all, delete these lines.
observe motor_overloaded_failed "the instrument behind motor_overloaded has failed or is disconnected"
doubt motor_overloaded_untrusted "motor_overloaded is not trusted while its instrument has failed" needs motor_overloaded_failed
motor_overloaded_untrusted undercuts motor_overload
claim motor_overloaded_blind "there is no trustworthy reading of motor_overloaded" needs motor_overloaded_failed

# TODO: confirm the device can tell when the motor_energized instrument has failed (a broken wire, a stuck
# or out-of-range value), and that show_motor_running is the right response then. If motor_energized is not an
# instrument at all, delete these lines.
observe motor_energized_failed "the instrument behind motor_energized has failed or is disconnected"
doubt motor_energized_untrusted "motor_energized is not trusted while its instrument has failed" needs motor_energized_failed
motor_energized_untrusted undercuts motor_running
claim motor_energized_blind "there is no trustworthy reading of motor_energized" needs motor_energized_failed
